Install Sensors.conf into the sysroot when cross-building

The sensorfw plugin installed it to an absolute /etc/xdg/QtProject, on the build host. It
belongs in the target's /etc/xdg/QtProject, where both QSensorManager (the last
ConfigLocation) and the plugin (QSettings system scope, XDG_CONFIG_DIRS) read it; it makes
sensorfw the default backend and lists the sensors the plugin registers.

diff --git a/src/plugins/sensors/sensorfw/sensorfw.pro b/src/plugins/sensors/sensorfw/sensorfw.pro
index 63a6611..9fd9d61 100644
--- a/src/plugins/sensors/sensorfw/sensorfw.pro
+++ b/src/plugins/sensors/sensorfw/sensorfw.pro
@@ -6,7 +6,8 @@ include(sensorfw.pri)
 QMAKE_USE += sensorfw
 
 CONFIGFILES.files = Sensors.conf
-CONFIGFILES.path = /etc/xdg/QtProject/
+# Cross builds: into the sysroot, not the build host's /etc.
+CONFIGFILES.path = $$[QT_SYSROOT]/etc/xdg/QtProject/
 INSTALLS += CONFIGFILES
 
 OTHER_FILES = plugin.json
